From: Altium-on-Wine kit
Subject: winemac.drv: match Altium GDI window backing stores to sRGB

Modules: dlls/winemac.drv
Base: wine-11.16 + existing kit mac-driver patches

Dense schematic panning spent most of the Cocoa main thread converting the
entire Retina GDI image to a different window backing color space. GDI surface
images are already tagged sRGB. Opt-in ALTIUM_MAC_SRGB=1 sets sRGB on new Cocoa
windows, retaining color management, Retina resolution and original image data.
The AD17 and AD26 launchers set this flag. AD17_SRGB_WINDOWS=0 or
AD26_SRGB_WINDOWS=0 restores the respective previous behavior.

--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
@@ -1078,6 +1078,13 @@
                                               defer:YES] autorelease];
 
         if (!window) return nil;
+
+        /* GDI surface images are 8-bit sRGB. Matching the window backing
+         * color space avoids a CPU conversion of every Retina pixel when
+         * Core Animation copies the image. ColorSync still maps the window
+         * to the display profile during composition. Opt-in for AD17. */
+        if ([[[NSProcessInfo processInfo] environment][@"ALTIUM_MAC_SRGB"] boolValue])
+            [window setColorSpace:[NSColorSpace sRGBColorSpace]];
 
         /* Standardize windows to eliminate differences between titled and
            borderless windows and between NSWindow and NSPanel. */
